# ── Rust build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/target
/target_*/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# ── Editor / OS cruft ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ── Runtime artifacts written to the working directory ───────────────────────
# Scene saves + terrain heightmap/splat sidecars (Phase 11.5F / 14F-3).
# Delete these lines if you want to commit a sample scene.
/scene.somnium
/scene.somnium.terrain*.bin

# Log output (engine traces, captured run output, etc.)
*.log

# ── AI-assisted development artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────
# Somnium is developed with AI assistance (Claude Code). The files below are the
# assistant's local configuration and its persistent session-memory / planning
# notes. They're useful while developing but are not part of the engine, and a
# couple contain personal working-style notes — so they stay out of the public
# repo. (Un-ignore any you'd rather publish; the engineering content they hold
# is also captured in context.md / ATTRIBUTION.md, which ARE committed.)
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
MEMORY.md
user_profile.md
feedback_approach.md
project_somnium.md
architecture_decisions.md
wgpu_api_gotchas.md
somnium_phase*.md
m2.md
m25.md

# Per-phase working records: plans, session hand-offs, measurement tables.
# Useful while a phase is in flight, and superseded by context.md once it
# closes — every conclusion that outlives the session it was written in is
# folded into context.md (and ATTRIBUTION.md for the study citations),
# which ARE committed. Keeping both would mean two accounts of the same
# decision drifting apart.
dev records/

# Phase CONTROL's audit is a regenerable contract rather than a transient
# hand-off. Keep its generator outputs/evidence manifest reviewable in-tree.
!dev records/
dev records/*
# Keep the top-level phase plans and index reviewable in Git. Per-phase working
# folders, hand-offs, audits and generated evidence remain ignored unless a
# narrower exception below explicitly preserves them.
!dev records/README.md
!dev records/phase_*.md
!dev records/phase_CONTROL.md
!dev records/phase CONTROL/
dev records/phase CONTROL/*
!dev records/phase CONTROL/CONTROL-A_reachability.md
!dev records/phase CONTROL/CONTROL-A_census.md
!dev records/phase CONTROL/CONTROL-B_property_seam.md
!dev records/phase CONTROL/CONTROL-C_asset_seam.md
!dev records/phase CONTROL/CONTROL-D_material_authoring.md
!dev records/phase CONTROL/README.md
!dev records/phase CONTROL/CONTROL-A_baseline/
dev records/phase CONTROL/CONTROL-A_baseline/*
!dev records/phase CONTROL/CONTROL-A_baseline/README.md
!dev records/phase CONTROL/CONTROL-A_baseline/*.png
!dev records/phase CONTROL/CONTROL-A_terrain_open.somtime

# Phase MORROWIND, same reasoning, and it should have been here from
# MORROWIND-A. The whole `phase MORROWIND/` folder was ignored for eleven
# sub-phases: the census, the Fyrox diff, the license audit, GHOSTFENCE's
# golden references and every per-sub-phase record existed only on one disk.
# The golden PNGs are the sharp end of it - a reference nobody else has is not
# a reference, and the gate that compares against it is unrunnable on a fresh
# clone. Found by MORROWIND-E2b, when `git add` of a golden refused.
!dev records/phase_MORROWIND.md
!dev records/phase MORROWIND/
dev records/phase MORROWIND/*
!dev records/phase MORROWIND/README.md
!dev records/phase MORROWIND/MORROWIND-*.md
# MORROWIND-AC evidence. Added with the sub-phase, per PORTAL-0-C's note that
# an allowlist silently swallows a phase whose entries were added afterwards.
!dev records/phase MORROWIND/AC/
dev records/phase MORROWIND/AC/*
!dev records/phase MORROWIND/AC/README.md
!dev records/phase MORROWIND/AC/AC_*.somtime
!dev records/phase MORROWIND/AC/AC_*.png
# Sub-phase measurements are source evidence; screenshots stay local unless
# promoted into the reviewed golden manifest below.
!dev records/phase MORROWIND/MORROWIND-AB_*.somtime
!dev records/phase MORROWIND/golden/
dev records/phase MORROWIND/golden/*
!dev records/phase MORROWIND/golden/manifest.json
!dev records/phase MORROWIND/golden/*.png

# Phase DOOM continuation. The original evidence folder predated the explicit
# phase allowlists above, so its records were local-only. Keep the reviewed
# index plus DOOM-D's matched timings and tone-mapped correctness captures.
!dev records/phase DOOM/
dev records/phase DOOM/*
!dev records/phase DOOM/README.md
!dev records/phase DOOM/DOOM-D.md
!dev records/phase DOOM/DOOM-D_*.somtime
!dev records/phase DOOM/DOOM-D_*.png
!dev records/phase DOOM/DOOM-G.md
!dev records/phase DOOM/DOOM-G_*.somtime
!dev records/phase DOOM/DOOM-G_*.png
!dev records/phase DOOM/DOOM-H.md
!dev records/phase DOOM/DOOM-H_*.somtime
!dev records/phase DOOM/DOOM-I.md
!dev records/phase DOOM/DOOM-I_*.somtime
!dev records/phase DOOM/DOOM-J.md
!dev records/phase DOOM/DOOM-J_*.somtime
!dev records/phase DOOM/DOOM-K.md
!dev records/phase DOOM/DOOM-K_*.somtime

# ── Phase PORTAL-0 (Source) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Same allowlist shape, and added in the same commit as the phase rather than
# after it: MORROWIND-E2b found that `dev records/phase MORROWIND/` had been
# ignored since MORROWIND-A, so the census, every sub-phase record and the plan
# itself existed on one disk and in no commit. A measurement phase whose
# evidence is untracked is a phase nobody can disagree with.
#
# The `.somtime` runs and the clipmap A/B captures are both source evidence
# here: `phase_PORTAL-0.md` §F's decision rests on the PNGs, not only on the
# timings, and a luminance gate quoted without the images it was computed from
# is an assertion.
!dev records/phase_PORTAL-0.md
!dev records/phase PORTAL-0/
dev records/phase PORTAL-0/*
!dev records/phase PORTAL-0/README.md
!dev records/phase PORTAL-0/PORTAL-0-*.somtime
!dev records/phase PORTAL-0/PORTAL-0-F_*.png

# Stray build output from a cargo invocation with the wrong working
# directory. `target/` at the root is already ignored; this catches the
# per-crate ones.
crates/*/target/

# ── Reference repositories (see ATTRIBUTION.md) ──────────────────────────────
# example_repo/ holds ~6 GB of third-party engines studied for architectural
# patterns only. It is excluded from the Cargo workspace and must NOT be pushed
# (size + redistribution licensing, e.g. the Unreal Engine EULA).
#
# EXCEPTION: somnium_physics_sys/build.rs compiles Jolt Physics (MIT) straight
# out of this tree, so the Jolt subdirectory is kept tracked — without it a
# fresh clone cannot build the physics crate.
example_repo/*
!example_repo/JoltPhysics-master/

# Transient capture logs from runtime verification scripts
st_*.log
st_*.err
rt_*.log
rt_*.err
sel.log
sel.err
*.somcap

# Phase 25K: Poly Haven source maps for the terrain materials. Re-derivable with
# tools/fetch_terrain_textures.sh; only the channel-packed result is committed.
assets/terrain/_source/
assets/terrain/bc7/
assets/.somnium/

# ── Graphify knowledge graph ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keep the portable query graph and its human-readable report. Everything else
# is regenerable cache/intermediate state or contains machine-local paths.
/.graphify-tool-venv/
/.graphify-uv-cache/
/graphify-out/*
!/graphify-out/graph.json
!/graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md
